Z||000023||Monkeyman||01-21-2001||07:39 AM||||Doc--I wondered about adding more memory, but Gateway said that I could easily do that anytime in the future.  GW would only allow $1400 credit (with the balance owed before it was shipped).  My current financial situation doesn't allow for alot of extra cash on hand, so I went this way.  I'll probably add memory later.<P>I paid $1400 and change for this outfit.  I probably could have gotten it slightly cheaper elsewhere, but like I said, GW was the only place offering any line of credit.  It's interesting to note how much cheaper computers have gotten in the last year or so.  About a year ago, I purchased my current computer for about the same amount of money (from GW, too).  The current one is/has:  <BR>DVD-ROM drive, but no CDRW<BR>20Mb hard drive<BR>64megs of RAM<BR>Celeron 400 processor<P>If computers keep dropping in price, I should be able to get that gov't supercomputer for around a grand in a few years. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||1
